 "intro": "Outside Lugdunum (Lyon), 19 February 197 AD. Clodius Albinus, governor of Britain, has crossed into Gaul and declared himself Emperor. You are Septimius Severus. Cassius Dio claims 150,000 men fought on each side.",
 "debrief": "In Cassius Dio’s account, Albinus’s right wing feigned retreat and lured Severus’s men into hidden pits. In the chaos, Severus’s horse was killed and he tore off his cloak and rallied his men on foot. The cavalry under Laetus, who some said was waiting to see who would win, finally charged and decided the battle. Albinus died, Lugdunum was sacked, and Severus ruled alone. The other choices are what-ifs.",
